  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "0",
      "text": "Sample code"
    },
    {
      "id": "1",
      "text": "If your contribution contains code, please make sure that it follows the\n{a1}Google coding style guide for JavaScript{/a1}.\nOtherwise, we will have to ask you to make changes, and that's no fun for anyone.",
      "attributes": {
        "a1": {
          "href": "https://google.github.io/styleguide/javascriptguide.xml"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "text": "Inline code"
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "text": "To indicate a span of code, wrap it with backtick quotes (`). Unlike a\npre-formatted code block, a code span indicates code within a normal paragraph.\nFor example:"
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "text": "{code1}Use the `printf()` function.\n{/code1}"
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "text": "Will result in:"
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "text": "Use the {code1}printf(){/code1} function."
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "text": "Code blocks"
    },
    {
      "id": "8",
      "text": "To produce a code block in Markdown, simply indent every line of the block by\nat least 4 spaces or 1 tab. For example, given this input:"
    },
    {
      "id": "9",
      "text": "{code1}Here is an example of AppleScript:\n\n    tell application \"Foo\"\n        beep\n    end tell\n{/code1}"
    },
    {
      "id": "10",
      "text": "will result in:"
    },
    {
      "id": "11",
      "text": "Here is an example of AppleScript:"
    },
    {
      "id": "12",
      "text": "{code1}tell application \"Foo\"\n    beep\nend tell\n{/code1}"
    },
    {
      "id": "13",
      "text": "Within a code block, ampersands ({code1}&#x26;{/code1}) and angle brackets ({code2}&#x3C;{/code2} and {code3}>{/code3}) are\nautomatically converted into HTML entities. This makes it very easy to include\nexample HTML source code using Markdown -- just paste it and indent it, and\nMarkdown will handle the hassle of encoding the ampersands and angle brackets."
    },
    {
      "id": "14",
      "text": "Warning: Wrapping code blocks in {code1}&#x26;amp;&#x26;lt;&#x26;gt;{/code1} is not supported on\nDevSite. DevSite will not automatically style these blocks and our integration\ntests will fail."
    },
    {
      "id": "15",
      "text": "Highlighting"
    },
    {
      "id": "16",
      "text": "Use {code1}&#x3C;strong>{/code1} to call attention to content within a {code2}&#x3C;pre>{/code2} block. Doing so\nwill lighten the surrounding content to emphasize the section highlighted by\nthe {code3}&#x3C;strong>{/code3} block. For example:"
    },
    {
      "id": "17",
      "text": "{code1}// ...\n// ...\n// ...\nfor (i = 0; i &#x3C; 10; i++) {\n    printf(\"Counting %d\\n\", i);\n\n    if (i % 3 == 0) {\n        someFunc(i);\n    }\n}\n// ...\n// ...\n// ...\n{/code1}"
    },
    {
      "id": "18",
      "text": "{code1}&#x3C;pre class=\"prettyprint\">\n// ...\n// ...\n// ...\nfor (i = 0; i &#x3C; 10; i++) {\n    printf(\"Counting %d\\n\", i);\n\n    &#x3C;strong>if (i % 3 == 0) {\n        someFunc(i);\n    }&#x3C;/strong>\n}\n// ...\n// ...\n// ...\n&#x3C;/pre>\n{/code1}"
    },
    {
      "id": "19",
      "text": "Click to copy"
    },
    {
      "id": "20",
      "text": "Click to copy is automatically enabled for all code blocks."
    },
    {
      "id": "21",
      "text": "Special Case: Templates - {{}}"
    },
    {
      "id": "22",
      "text": "If you need to include templates in your code samples, be sure to escape them."
    },
    {
      "id": "23",
      "text": "For example:"
    },
    {
      "id": "24",
      "text": "{code1}&#x3C;pre class=\"prettyprint\">\n&#x26;lt;polymer-media-query query=\"max-width:640px\" queryMatches=\"&#x26;#123;{isPhone}}\">\n&#x3C;/pre>\n{/code1}"
    },
    {
      "id": "25",
      "text": "If it's inline, you'll need to wrap it in a {code1}&#x3C;code>{/code1} block instead of backticks."
    },
    {
      "id": "26",
      "text": "{code1}* Declarative two-way data-binding: &#x3C;code>&#x3C;input id=\"input\" value=\"&#x26;#123;{foo}}\">&#x3C;/code>\n{/code1}"
    }
  ]
}
